<!--ID=B7267351-473F-409D-9765-754A8EBCDE05;Version=1|{"VoiceNameToIdMapItems":[{"Id":"f1b99834-fbfc-4d32-846d-c4dbd3050c19","Name":"Microsoft Server Speech Text to Speech Voice (en-GB, OllieMultilingualNeural)","ShortName":"en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural","Locale":"en-GB","VoiceType":"StandardVoice"}]}-->
<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.50%" pitch="-2.50%">
            But now thus says the Lord, he who created you, he who formed you.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            Fear not, for I have redeemed you.
            <break time="500ms"/>
            I have called you by name.
            <break time="500ms"/>
            You are mine.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            He who created you. He who formed you. These are not coincidental words. The God speaking here is the same God who made you — who thought you into being, who knew your shape before you took it.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            And that God says: I have called you by name.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            There is something that happens when someone knows your name. Not just your face in a crowd. Not just a general awareness that you exist. They know you. They call you. They are speaking specifically, personally, to you and no one else.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            God does not shout at a crowd and hope you hear. He speaks your name. He has always known it. He spoke it before you were born. And He speaks it still — over your fear, over your doubt, over the nights when you wonder whether any of this is real.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            I have called you by name.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            You are mine.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            Belonging. That is what this word carries. Not ownership in the cold sense — not a transaction. Belonging in the truest sense. You are His. You come under His care. His attention. His protection. His love.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            I have redeemed you.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            The word means bought back. Recovered. Brought home from a far place. Whatever distance you have felt — whatever has accumulated between you and God — He has already moved to close it. The work is His. The cost was His. The coming home is yours.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            You are known. You are called. You belong to Him.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            Rest in that tonight.
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
